{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the failing-snapshot receipt and replaced the constructor question's last reachability limitation with that observed trigger. Receipt 49444692e9db40dd84b1aa3c6d603193 shows the node's snapshot attempts failing four times and being tolerated, its last snapshot never advancing while about 8300 committed entries accumulate above it, and the feature-on restart then never finishing within the window (violated, witness index 1), while the same stores restarted without the feature returned and stayed at the snapshot index (holds, index 3), reported the observed 128-slot capacity against a 130-batch demand (holds, index 3), and left the other two voters with a quorum (holds, index 2). I acquired the snapshot loop's error handling as a source, recorded the tolerated-failure behaviour as new knowledge with the receipt, extended the stall fact's conditions and executions, and rewrote the question account so the trigger is an operationally realistic snapshot-store failure at default batch settings rather than a harness-chosen interval; the earlier delayed-snapshot receipt remains as the second observed route. Remaining limits recorded: the failing store is a harness wrapper and only Create failures are injected, non-return is observed over a bounded window with permanence argued from source, in-memory stores with a graceful shutdown and an abandoned stalled constructor without supervision. Incomplete: the term-changing truncation repair path for the split-brain chain.\"}"}}
